  "findings": [
    "Seed-only gap-50 recovery on 0.1.0-alpha.4 reproduced custody's full Qi coin set exactly (49 coins, 16,307 Qits), found all three conversion recipients, and kept the 3,416 credited Qits locked until 10,338,942-10,339,111.",
    "Specialized-fee quotes, authenticated backup restore with wrong-password rejection, bounded WQUAI log decoding and transaction interchange round trips all passed on 0.1.0-alpha.4.",
    "The 98.6-hour head soak (alpha.3-era binary) followed 71,074 blocks through 152 reorgs of at most two blocks. Its three ReplayHistoryUnavailable errors cannot have been lost history with 4,096 retained anchors. They fit a page read that missed a block at or below the tip it had just read, which is the case fabfdc6 now retries as ObservationChanged. The log does not show which read returned null.",
    "Two check runs failed transiently: a JSON-RPC -32000 on getLogs and an RPC timeout. Both passed on an immediate rerun. The gateway answered in about 0.15 s between them.",
    "locked-spend was not rerun: it assumes every coin is locked, and the wallet now holds spendable Qi."
  ]
